title Vinyl: the output muted (the launcher's mute key, another app, pactl): the level box takes the muted look (dark, white) with the speaker-off mark and "Mute" where both fit, else the mark alone, large; never the level, never another word; "-" does nothing, "+" brings the sound back at its level (640x480: qa-640-muted, qa-deck-muted; 480x320 and 320x480: qa-muted-small; a board without a sound server: qa-soft-muted)
sizes 800x480 480x480 720x720 480x800 480x640
env VINYL_DEMO 1
env VINYL_DEMO_STATE playing
env VINYL_DEMO_MUTED 1

wait 1200
shot 01-now-muted
expect esc
expect notext "60"
# the muted box as drawn (the owner, 2026-11-13: "no need for the word muted if it doesn't fit the speaker off glyph is
# enough", "Mute is better than Muted"): "Mute" beside the mark where both fit at CAPTION or larger, else the mark alone
# (24 px or more, drawn about 60 % of the box high: the app stops a scene that breaks it, check_mute_fit); qa-info.txt's
# muted= line is read from these lines and the app's own log of the box
@800x480,720x720,480x800 expect text "Mute"
@480x480,480x640 expect notext "Mute"
expect notext "Muted"
expect notext "Off"
wait 300
shot 02-now-muted-volume
expect notext "60"
# "-" while muted does nothing
@800x480 tapxy 0.749 0.848
@480x480 tapxy 0.629 0.922
@720x720 tapxy 0.636 0.919
@480x800 tapxy 0.486 0.936
@480x640 tapxy 0.489 0.928
wait 300
expect notext "60"
@800x480,720x720,480x800 expect text "Mute"
# "+" brings the sound back at its level
@800x480 tapxy 0.921 0.848
@480x480 tapxy 0.881 0.922
@720x720 tapxy 0.901 0.919
@480x800 tapxy 0.849 0.936
@480x640 tapxy 0.809 0.928
wait 300
shot 03-now-unmuted
expect notext "Mute"
expect text "60"
expect noquit
